          "id": "day1_page06_commentary",
          "type": "commentary",
          "title": "What the Feathered Thing Is",
          "bodyMarkdown": "Dickinson refuses to define hope as a feeling. Instead it is a small creature — “the thing with feathers” — that *perches*, settling in to stay, inside the soul, singing a wordless tune that “never stops - at all.” Hope here needs no reasons; it simply keeps singing.",
