          "type": "poet_background",
          "title": "Who Was Emily Dickinson?",
          "bodyMarkdown": "Emily Dickinson (1830–1886) lived almost her whole life in her family's house in Amherst, Massachusetts. Famously private, she wrote close to 1,800 poems but published only a handful, anonymously, while she was alive. This is among her most beloved.",
