          "id": "day2_page06_commentary",
          "type": "commentary",
          "title": "Sweetest in the Storm",
          "bodyMarkdown": "Now the paradox: the bird is heard “sweetest - in the Gale.” Hope sings most beautifully in the worst weather. Only a “sore” — a grievous — storm could “abash” (shame into silence) this “little Bird that kept so many warm.” It is small, but unshaken, and you are far from the first it has warmed.",
          "prompt": null,
          "chunkIds": [],
          "roundType": null,
          "estimatedSeconds": 60,
          "metadata": {},
          "orderIndex": 5
        },
        {
