          "type": "commentary",
          "title": "It Asked No Crumb",
          "bodyMarkdown": "The speaker testifies in the first person: she has carried this bird to the “chillest land” and “strangest Sea” — the edges of cold and strangeness — “Yet - never - in Extremity, / It asked a crumb - of me.” The bird that warms and sings demands no payment. That is the poem's quiet gift.",
          "prompt": null,
          "chunkIds": [],
          "roundType": null,
          "estimatedSeconds": 60,
